id: pm-n13lzc
title: "GH-739: expose duplicate-cluster discovery as a first-class CLI and SDK workflow"
description: "GitHub: https://github.com/unbraind/pm-cli/issues/739. Create-time similarity advice does not let agents sweep duplicate clusters that already exist. Promote the existing canonical batch duplicate-cluster SDK primitive into bounded CLI, MCP, and PmClient surfaces with token-efficient summaries and canonical-item remediation guidance."
type: Issue
status: closed
priority: 1
tags: []
created_at: "2026-07-26T12:13:36.253Z"
updated_at: "2026-07-26T19:51:34.196Z"
closed_at: "2026-07-26T19:43:51.671Z"
claim_principal: "harness:codex#de74a49829faaec73e28ece0"
author: "harness:codex"
acceptance_criteria: "CLI, MCP, and typed SDK consumers can list existing duplicate clusters without creating an item; output is bounded and deterministic; cluster provenance and canonical merge/close guidance reuse existing duplicate governance."
parent: pm-usfg
resolution: "Bounded duplicate-cluster discovery shipped across CLI, MCP, PmClient, and public SDK."
expected_result: Agents can discover existing duplicate clusters without creating items and receive deterministic bounded remediation guidance.
actual_result: All-status/status/since/threshold/limit discovery returns deterministic canonical clusters and safe close commands through every public transport.
